## Project Description

A Django-based **URL Shortener** application that allows users to:

- ✨ Create **short URLs** for long URLs
- 📊 Track the number of clicks per URL
- 🖥 Manage URLs in a **user dashboard**
- 🔗 Redirect short URLs to the original URLs
- 🕵️ View click details including **IP, browser, platform, and device**

---

## User Authentication & Profile Features

- 📝 **User Registration** with username, email, and password
- 🔐 **Login** and Logout functionality
- 🛠 **Profile Update** (username, email, first name, last name)
- 🔑 **Password Change** with old password verification
- 💻 Bootstrap 5 styled forms with validation
- 📢 Flash messages for feedback

---

## URL Shortening Features

- 🔹 Create **short URLs** with unique 6-character or 10-character UIDs
- ✏️ **Edit** or **delete** your own URLs
- 📈 Auto-increment click count per URL
- 🔄 Redirect short URL to the original URL safely
- ⚡ **AJAX support** for dynamic URL creation, editing, and deletion

---

## Click Tracking Features

- 🌐 Records **IP address, browser, platform, and device** for each click
- 📋 Click details displayed per URL for logged-in users
- ❌ Ability to **delete individual click records**
- 🛠 Admin panel support for viewing click history

---

## Admin Panel Features

- Full management of `Url` and `UrlClick` models
- 🔎 **Search** and **filter** URLs and clicks
- 📊 Click counts and URL preview directly in admin
- 🔗 Clickable short URL links in admin

---

## Technologies Used

| Technology | Purpose |
|------------|---------|
| Python 3.8+ | Backend logic |
| Django 3.x/4.x | Web framework |
| SQLite / PostgreSQL | Database |
| Bootstrap 5 | Front-end styling |
| HTML / CSS / JS | Web UI |
| user-agents | Detect browser / device info |

---

## Setup Instructions

```bash
# Clone the repository
git clone https://github.com/vishnuvm1122/url-shortner.git

# Navigate into project folder
cd url-shortner

# Create virtual environment
python3 -m venv venv

# Activate environment (Linux/macOS)
source venv/bin/activate

# Activate environment (Windows)
venv\Scripts\activate

# Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# Apply migrations
python manage.py migrate

# Create superuser
python manage.py createsuperuser

# Run development server
python manage.py runserver
```

